      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can use the formula for the average number of rounds played: average = sum of all rounds played / total number of golfers.\n\nIn this case, we have the following information:\n- Number of golfers who played 1 round of golf: 5\n- Number of golfers who played 2 rounds of golf: 2\n- Number of golfers who played 3 rounds of golf: 2\n- Number of golfers who played 4 rounds of golf: 3\n- Number of golfers who played 5 rounds of golf: 5\n\nWe can then plug these values into the formula to find the average:\n\naverage = (5 rounds * 5 golfers + 2 rounds * 2 golfers + 3 rounds * 3 golfers + 4 rounds * 5 golfers) / 15 golfers\n\naverage = (25 + 4 + 9 + 20) / 15\n\naverage = 58 / 15 = 3.8666...\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number, the average number of rounds played by each golfer is $\\boxed{4}$.The answer is: 4",
